==English==

===Etymology===
{{compound|en|sea|food}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsiːfuːd/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

#A colloquial term for [[fish]], [[shellfish]], [[seaweed]], and other [[edible]] aquatic life.
#A nutritional term and culinary term for [[finned fish]] and [[shellfish]] used as food. In some cultures [[cartilaginous fish]] may be included. Contextually, other aquatic animals like [[tetrapods]] and aquatic plants like [[seaweed]] are excluded from the definition. In the nutritional context, culinary context and in some regional vernacular the term “seafood” is ordinarily differentiated from [[meat|“meat”]], which is defined as a separate category of food. 
#A general term and regional vernacular for edible marine fish and shellfish. In this context “seafood” is sometimes not deemed as its own food category; rather its considered to be a specific subcategory of meat when the broader definitions of “meat” are being used.

